# Commit Message Format

## Structure

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[body — optional]
```

## Types

| Type | When to use |
|---|---|
| `feat` | new feature, new skill, new script |
| `fix` | fix incorrect behavior |
| `refactor` | refactor (no behavior change) |
| `test` | test cases |
| `chore` | config, maintenance, dependency updates |
| `docs` | documentation, examples, explanations |
| `ci` | CI/CD pipeline changes |

## Scope

Fill in the smallest meaningful scope of the change, not limited to skill names, e.g.:

- skill: `open-qa-bug`, `version-test-plan`, `write-bdd`, `tc-merge`
- rules: `rules`, `gherkin`
- automation: `e2e`, `scripts`, `ci`
- config: `config`, `deps`
- docs: `docs`, `examples`

If it spans multiple scopes, omit the scope or use the closest parent name.

## Rules

- All English, imperative verbs (`add` not `added`)
- subject ≤ 72 characters, no trailing period
- wrap body at 72 characters; explain the "why", not the "what"

## Examples

```
feat(open-qa-bug): add impact and root cause sections to bug report
fix(bdd): correct gherkin rule reference path
refactor(version-test-plan): extract output templates to references/
chore(rules): add git commit and pr message format
feat(e2e): add smoke test steps for video watch flow
ci: add GitHub Actions workflow for automated test run
docs(open-qa-bug): add 3 web-adapted bug report examples
```
